1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,320
Good morning everyone. My name's Joy Parkins and I'm the restaurant manager.

2
00:00:08,320 --> 00:00:14,410
And I understand that none of you have had any previous experience as kitchen assistants.

3
00:00:14,410 --> 00:00:17,220
Well, you might be feeling a bit nervous now

4
00:00:17,220 --> 00:00:21,690
but most of our kitchen assistants say they enjoy the work.

5
00:00:21,690 --> 00:00:25,529
OK, they might get shouted at sometimes, but it's nothing personal,

6
00:00:25,529 --> 00:00:29,400
and they're pleased that they have so many different things to do

7
00:00:29,460 --> 00:00:31,810
which means they never get bored.

8
00:00:31,810 --> 00:00:35,936
And I'll tell you straightaway that if you do well,

9
00:00:35,936 --> 00:00:41,300
we might think about moving you up and giving you some more responsibility.

10
00:00:41,300 --> 00:00:47,220
Right, well, you've all shown up on time, which is an excellent start.

11
00:00:47,220 --> 00:00:51,333
Now I'm glad to see none of you have unsuitable footwear,

12
00:00:51,333 --> 00:00:57,690
so that's good - you need to be careful as the floors can get very wet and slippery.

13
00:00:57,690 --> 00:01:02,426
Those of you with long hair have got it well out of the way,

14
00:01:02,426 --> 00:01:05,680
but some of you'll need to remove your rings and bracelets

15
00:01:06,120 --> 00:01:08,516
just put them somewhere safe for today,

16
00:01:08,516 --> 00:01:13,590
and remember to leave them at home tomorrow, as they can be a safety hazard.

17
00:01:13,590 --> 00:01:18,048
Now it's going to be a busy day for you all today -

18
00:01:18,048 --> 00:01:23,620
we don't have any tables free for this evening, and only a few for lunch.

19
00:01:23,620 --> 00:01:26,195
Fortunately we've got our Head Chef back -

20
00:01:26,195 --> 00:01:32,080
he was away on holiday all last week which meant the other chefs had extra work.

21
00:01:32,080 --> 00:01:35,620
Now, I'll tell you a bit more about the job in a minute

22
00:01:36,040 --> 00:01:39,330
but first, some general regulations.

23
00:01:39,330 --> 00:01:42,800
For all of you, whatever your age

24
00:01:43,120 --> 00:01:47,970
there's some equipment you mustn't use until you've been properly trained,

25
00:01:47,970 --> 00:01:53,730
like the waste disposal system for example, for health and safety reasons.

26
00:01:53,730 --> 00:01:57,700
Then I think there are two of you here who are under 18

27
00:01:58,600 --> 00:02:01,670
that's Emma and Jake, isn't it?

28
00:02:01,670 --> 00:02:07,360
Right. so for you two, the meat slicer is out of bounds.

29
00:02:07,360 --> 00:02:14,830
And of course none of you are allowed to use the electric mixer until you've been shown how it works.

30
00:02:14,830 --> 00:02:19,260
Now you may have heard that this can be a stressful job

31
00:02:19,260 --> 00:02:23,060
and I have to say that can be true.

32
00:02:23,060 --> 00:02:26,495
You'll be working an eight-hour day for the first week,

33
00:02:26,495 --> 00:02:31,990
though you'll have the chance to do overtime after that as well if you want to.

34
00:02:31,990 --> 00:02:37,090
But however long the hours are, you'll get a break in the middle.

35
00:02:37,090 --> 00:02:41,655
What you will find is that you're on your feet all day long,

36
00:02:41,655 --> 00:02:46,220
lifting and carrying, so if you're not fit now you soon will be!

37
00:02:46,220 --> 00:02:50,081
You'll find you don't have much chance to take it easy -

38
00:02:50,081 --> 00:02:54,644
when someone tells you to do something you need to do it straightaway -

39
00:02:54,644 --> 00:03:00,260
but at least we do have a very efficient air conditioning system compared with some kitchens.

40
00:03:00,260 --> 00:03:04,470
Now let me tell you about some of the people you need to know.

41
00:03:04,470 --> 00:03:09,080
So as I said, I'm Joy Parkins and I decide

42
00:03:09,080 --> 00:03:13,080
who does what during the day and how long they work for.

43
00:03:13,080 --> 00:03:18,380
I'll be trying to get you to work with as many different people in the kitchen as possible,

44
00:03:18,380 --> 00:03:21,030
so that you learn while you're on the job.

45
00:03:21,030 --> 00:03:26,520
One person whose name you must remember is David Field.

46
00:03:26,520 --> 00:03:30,597
If you injure yourself at all, even if it's really minor,

47
00:03:30,597 --> 00:03:34,740
you must report to him and he'll make sure the incident is recorded

48
00:03:34,740 --> 00:03:37,640
and you get the appropriate treatment.

49
00:03:37,640 --> 00:03:41,180
He's trained to give basic treatment to staff himself

50
00:03:41,260 --> 00:03:44,440
or he'll send you off somewhere else if necessary.

51
00:03:44,440 --> 00:03:48,880
Then there's Dexter Wills - he's the person you need to see

52
00:03:48,880 --> 00:03:52,160
if you smash a plate or something like that.

53
00:03:52,160 --> 00:03:56,012
Don't just leave it and hope no one will notice -

54
00:03:56,012 --> 00:03:58,340
it's really important to get things noted

55
00:03:58,340 --> 00:04:01,790
and replaced or there could be problems later.

56
00:04:01,790 --> 00:04:05,050
And finally, there's Mike Smith.

57
00:04:05,050 --> 00:04:09,978
He's the member of staff who takes care of all the stores of perishables,

58
00:04:09,978 --> 00:04:14,554
so if you notice we're getting low in flour or sugar or something,

59
00:04:14,554 --> 00:04:19,130
make sure you let him know so he can put in an order.

60
00:04:19,130 --> 00:04:22,390
OK, now the next thing...
